{{define "content"}}
<article style="max-width: 800px;">
  <h1 class="mb-3">Privacy Policy</h1>

  <div class="alert alert-warning">
    <strong>Template content, not legal advice.</strong> This page is placeholder text generated for
    this project and has not been reviewed by an attorney. Before using it with real users, have it
    reviewed and customized by a qualified lawyer for your jurisdiction, and confirm it accurately
    describes your actual data practices.
  </div>

  <p class="text-muted">Last updated: {{currentYear}}</p>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4">1. Scope</h2>
  <p>
    This policy describes how resumebank.biz (the "Service") collects, uses, discloses, and
    protects personal data belonging to candidates, employers, and visitors, and explains the
    privacy rights available to you under applicable law, including the EU/UK General Data
    Protection Regulation ("GDPR") and the California Consumer Privacy Act as amended by the
    California Privacy Rights Act ("CCPA/CPRA").
  </p>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4">2. Data Controller and Contact</h2>
  <p>
    The site operator is the data controller responsible for personal data processed through the
    Service. Questions, requests, or complaints about this policy can be directed to the site
    operator's published contact information.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4">3. Personal Data We Collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account data:</strong> email address, password (stored as a salted hash, never in plain text), and account role.</li>
    <li><strong>Candidate profile data:</strong> name, title, location, phone, email, LinkedIn URL, skills, summary, resume content, uploaded resume/files, and an optional profile picture.</li>
    <li><strong>Employer profile data:</strong> company name, industry, location, phone, contact email, website, description, and an optional company logo.</li>
    <li><strong>Job posting data:</strong> job details submitted by employers, including the chosen application method (a URL or contact email).</li>
    <li><strong>Usage data:</strong> messages sent between candidates and employers, job votes, and search activity.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address and standard web server logs, and strictly-necessary cookies (see Section 6).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4">4. How We Use Your Data and Legal Basis</h2>
  <table class="table table-sm table-bordered">
    <thead><tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis (GDPR Art. 6)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Creating and authenticating your account</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Publishing your candidate or employer profile and job postings</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Full-text search and AI-assisted candidate/job matching</td><td>Performance of a contract; legitimate interest</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Delivering messages between candidates and employers</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Sending password reset and account-related emails</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Securing the Service and preventing abuse</td><td>Legitimate interest</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4" id="cookies">5. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The Service uses only strictly-necessary cookies required for it to function. It does not use
    advertising, analytics, or tracking cookies, and does not use cookies to build cross-site
    advertising profiles.
  </p>
  <table class="table table-sm table-bordered">
    <thead><tr><th>Cookie</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Type</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>resumebank_session</code></td><td>Keeps you signed in to your candidate/employer account</td><td>Strictly necessary</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>resumebank_admin_session</code></td><td>Keeps site administrators signed in to the admin panel</td><td>Strictly necessary</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>resumebank_csrf</code></td><td>Protects forms against cross-site request forgery</td><td>Strictly necessary</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Because these cookies are necessary for the Service to operate, they are set without requesting
    prior consent, consistent with the ePrivacy exemption for strictly-necessary cookies. You can
    block or delete cookies in your browser settings, but doing so will prevent you from staying
    signed in.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4">6. How We Share Your Data</h2>
  <p>
    Candidate profiles, resumes, and uploaded files are public by design so employers can find and
    contact candidates &mdash; do not upload anything you don't want publicly visible. Employer
    profiles and job postings are likewise public. We share data with the following categories of
    service providers strictly to operate the Service: our hosting provider, our transactional
    email provider (for password reset emails), and, for the AI-assisted matching feature, a
    self-hosted language model that does not send your data to a third party.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal data to third parties, and we do not share personal data with third
    parties for cross-context behavioral advertising. See Section 9 for the formal CCPA/CPRA
    disclosure.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4">7. Data Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We retain your account and profile data for as long as your account is active. If you'd like
    your account and associated data deleted, contact the site operator using the published contact
    information.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4" id="your-rights">8. Your Rights Under GDPR</h2>
  <p>If you are located in the EU/UK, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
    <li>Correct inaccurate or incomplete data (most profile fields can be edited directly on your profile)</li>
    <li>Request erasure of your data ("right to be forgotten")</li>
    <li>Restrict or object to certain processing</li>
    <li>Receive your data in a portable format</li>
    <li>Withdraw consent at any time, where processing is based on consent</li>
    <li>Lodge a complaint with your local data protection supervisory authority</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To exercise any of these rights, contact the site operator using the published contact information.</p>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4" id="do-not-sell">9. California Privacy Rights (CCPA/CPRA)</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information:</strong> resumebank.biz does not sell
    personal information for monetary or other valuable consideration, and does not share personal
    information with third parties for cross-context behavioral advertising, as those terms are
    defined under the CCPA/CPRA. Because we do not engage in either practice, no opt-out action is
    required &mdash; but if you would still like to submit a Do Not Sell/Share request, or if you
    are a California resident wishing to exercise your right to know, delete, or correct your
    personal information, contact the site operator using the published contact information and we
    will honor your request. We will not discriminate against you for exercising any of these
    rights.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4">10. International Data Transfers</h2>
  <p>
    The Service's infrastructure may be located in a different country than you. Where personal
    data is transferred internationally, we rely on appropriate safeguards required by applicable
    law.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4">11. Data Security</h2>
  <p>
    Passwords are hashed with bcrypt and never stored in plain text. We use reasonable technical
    and organizational measures to protect personal data, but no method of transmission or storage
    is completely secure.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4">12. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>The Service is not directed at, and is not intended for use by, anyone under the age of 16.</p>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4">13. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. Continued use of the Service after changes are
    posted constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h5 mt-4">14. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy, or requests to exercise your privacy rights, can be directed to
    the site operator's published contact information.
  </p>
</article>
{{end}}

